{"url": "https://www.monash.edu/science/schools/earth-atmosphere-environment", "final_url": "https://www.monash.edu/science/schools/earth-atmosphere-environment", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-31", "text": "Home\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nPrevious menu\nToggle navigation\nSCIENCE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nHome\nMonash Australia\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nSTAFF\nStaff\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTAFF\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTUDENTS\nStudents\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nSTUDENTS\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nALUMNI\nAlumni\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nALUMNI\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nSEARCH\nSCIENCE\nABOUT US\nFUTURE STUDENTS\nCURRENT STUDENTS\nRESEARCH\nMORE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nSchool of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment\nPrevious\nEARTH, ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nEducating the next generation of scientists to provide the solutions urgently required to address the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.\nASSOCIATE PROFESSOR KATHRYN FITZSIMMONS\nBe brave and don\u2019t be daunted.\nRead more\nNext\n12\nSchool of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment\nFrom the red plains of Broken Hill to Antarctica, we study the Earth\u2019s core, its atmosphere and everything in between. A new, hands-on way to explore and learn earth sciences.\nMonash University is ranked 31st in the world for 2027 (QS)\nThe school subjects are ranked:\nAtmospheric Science - 46th (ARWC Subject Rankings 2027)\nGeography - 51-100th (QS Subject Rankings 2027)\nGeology, Geophysics - 47th (QS Subject rankings 2027)\nEnvironmental Sciences - 52nd (QS Subject rankings 2027)\nCURRENT STUDENTS\nProbe the challenges of the earth\nEXPLORE YOUR OPTIONS\n.\nFUTURE STUDENTS\nExplore your possibilites\nEXPLORE MORE\n.\nHonours degrees\nEnhance your degree with honours. VIEPS Courses\nMaster of Science\nA course tailored for the professional scientist.\nPostgraduate degrees\nWhether you think global or local, a PhD equips you to help your community.\nResearch\nUnlock the mysteries of our planet \u2013 from its core to its atmosphere.\nFacilities\nState-of-the-art learning facilities.\nUpcoming events\nStay in the loop. Register for conferences, seminars, symposiums and workshops.\nGeography at Monash\nMake geography part of your undergraduate degree at Monash\nAbout us\nOur people\nEquity, Diversity & Inclusion Committee\nContact us\nQuick links\nLatest news\nSchool intranet\nNewsletter\nCode of Conduct\nLatest news from School of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment\nFrom deep within the Earth to the global energy transition, Monash Science is helping shape the future of critical minerals\nMonash University's scientific leadership in critical minerals research took centre stage as an international diplomatic delegation representing more than 30 countries visited the University's world-class research facilities on Wednesday 28 October.\nEARTH ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nWorld-first global sand dunes map reveals clues to distant worlds, including Mars\nA new study from Monash University has delivered the most complete and accurate digital map of Earth\u2019s wind-blown sand dunes to date.\nEARTH ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nInvisible microbes \u2018mining\u2019 toxic waste in the Flinders Ranges\nMonash University scientists found microscopic life breaking down decades-old mining waste in South Australia, converting stable radioactive and toxic metals into mobile nanoparticles.\nEARTH ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nNew study sheds light on Victoria\u2019s future rainfall\nThe study highlights the important role of natural climate variability in shaping recent rainfall patterns, and how this influences expectations for the future.\nEARTH ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nCopper\u2019s \u201cgatekeeper\u201d could unlock cleaner energy future\nA common mineral hiding in plain sight could hold the key to making copper production cleaner, faster and more efficient, just as global demand for the metal surges to power the energy transition.\nEARTH ATMOSPHERE AND ENVIRONMENT\nView more articles\nWe acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians\nCOMMUNITY\nFaculties\nLocations\nDiversity and inclusion\nSafety and security\nSustainability\nRESOURCES\nImportant dates\nHow to apply\nA-Z index\nPolicy Bank\nFAQs\nCONTACT\nContact us\nCampus maps\nJobs at Monash\nRecruit a student\nPay online\nNEWS\nLatest news\nMonash Lens\nPodcasts\nA Different Lens\nMonash Life\nON OUR SITE\nCurrent students\nStaff intranet\nSite map\nREGISTERED AUSTRALIAN UNIVERSITY\nABN: 12 377 614 012\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140\nCRICOS PROVIDER NUMBER\nMonash University: 00008C\nMonash College: 01857J\nAUTHORISED BY\nExecutive Director, Marketing\nWebsite feedback\nLast updated: Oct 2026\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & copyright\nTerms & conditions\nData privacy & cyber security\nData Consent Settings\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Monash University\nWe use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions\nAccept all\nCookie settings", "links": [["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["Courses", "https://www.monash.edu/study/courses"], ["Monash Online", "https://online.monash.edu/"], ["Library", "https://www.monash.edu/library"], ["Donate", "https://www.monash.edu/giving"], ["Science", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["Scho